      "content": "Fine, I'll upload the transcript for Marcus Vane right now since you're being difficult about access. \n\n[Transcript Uploaded: Marcus Vane - Initial Screening]\nVane: \"I believe the best results come from a meticulously planned strategy. I prefer to ensure all stakeholders are aligned before moving into execution to prevent costly errors. While I can pivot when necessary, I find that high-chaos environments often lead to avoidable inefficiencies that I prefer to minimize through structure.\"\n\nThere. There's the transcript. Read it. Now, look at the culture I described—aggressive, fast-paced, high-pressure. Be honest: does this guy actually fit that, or is he going to be a bottleneck for us because he's too focused on \"planning\" and \"alignment\"? I need a straight answer so I can decide whether to keep him in the running.",
